[1m[38;2;255;169;64marmada guild — you, portable: machine-global, and synced between your machines[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mVERBS[0m
  init             [38;2;107;114;128mbuild your guild by interviewing you[0m
  pull             [38;2;107;114;128mbring this machine's guild up to date[0m
  push             [38;2;107;114;128msend local guild changes to the remote[0m
  export           [38;2;107;114;128mwrite the whole guild to one portable file[0m
  import <bundle>  [38;2;107;114;128mrestore a guild from a bundle[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mNOT BUILT YET[0m
  edit    [38;2;107;114;128mopen a guild file, validate it, commit it[0m
  verify  [38;2;107;114;128mcross-check every workflow, skill and scope[0m

`armada guild <verb> --help` for one verb's usage and flags.

Your guild is how you work: your voice, your skills, your workflows. Set it up
once and it follows you — a new laptop is a `pull` rather than an afternoon.

It never lands in a project's history, and what is only true of this machine
stays on it: its settings, its database, and the Jobs running here.
